  "ledHelpTileHelp": "What the lights on the sensor mean",
  "ledHelpTitle": "LED signals",
  "ledHelpIntro": "The sensor has an orange and a red light. Both sit right next to each other in the same tiny part, so they are easy to mix up. The orange one shows what the sensor is doing, the red one belongs to charging. The bars below show each signal over about two seconds: the coloured part means the light is on.",
  "ledOrangeSection": "Orange light",
  "ledWaitingTitle": "Slow blinking",
  "ledWaitingTiming": "0.3 s on, 0.7 s off, repeating",
  "ledWaitingMeaning": "The sensor is awake and waiting for the app. The app connects by itself once the sensor is paired.",
  "ledConnectedTitle": "On all the time",
  "ledConnectedTiming": "Steady light",
  "ledConnectedMeaning": "The app is connected. The sensor does not go to sleep while it is connected.",
  "ledGoingToSleepTitle": "6 quick blinks, then off",
  "ledGoingToSleepTiming": "0.15 s on, 0.15 s off, 6 times",
  "ledGoingToSleepMeaning": "The sensor is going to sleep to save battery. This happens after 1 minute without a connected app and without a jump.",
  "ledAsleepTitle": "Off",
  "ledAsleepTiming": "No light",
  "ledAsleepMeaning": "The sensor is asleep and the app cannot find it. Shake or hit the sensor to wake it up: it reacts within about 4 seconds. If nothing happens, the battery may be empty.",
  "ledWokeUpTitle": "3 short blinks, then slow blinking",
  "ledWokeUpTiming": "0.08 s on, 0.08 s off, 3 times",
  "ledWokeUpMeaning": "The sensor noticed the movement and woke up. It is now waiting for the app.",
  "ledErrorTitle": "Fast blinking that does not stop",
  "ledErrorTiming": "0.1 s on, 0.1 s off, without end",
  "ledErrorMeaning": "The sensor could not start and does not work. Press the reset button on the sensor or disconnect and reconnect its power.",
  "ledRedSection": "Red light (charging)",
  "ledRedBody": "The red light belongs to the charging chip, not to the sensor software. It only works while the sensor is plugged in via USB: on battery power it is always off. It says nothing about the connection to the app.",
  "ledChargingTitle": "Short flash about once a second",
  "ledChargingTiming": "0.16 s on, 1.12 s off, repeating",
  "ledChargingMeaning": "The battery is charging. The last part of charging is slow: the light can keep flashing for half an hour or more while the app already shows over 90 %.",
  "ledChargedTitle": "On for just under a minute, then off",
  "ledChargedTiming": "Steady light for about 50 s",
  "ledChargedMeaning": "The battery is full. After that the light stays off, even though USB is still connected.",
  "ledChargeOffTitle": "Off while plugged in",
  "ledChargeOffTiming": "No light",
  "ledChargeOffMeaning": "Usually the battery is full. If the sensor was just plugged in and the red light never came on, check the cable and the power source. The light can start flashing again later when the charger tops the battery up.",
  "ledRedSource": "These signals are taken from the data sheet of the charging chip. On our own sensors only the flashing while charging has been seen so far, so the other two may differ slightly. The app cannot show whether the sensor is charging, because the sensor software cannot read this light.",
